        content: `**Patient**: David, 32-year-old male, brought to ED by EMS after **acetaminophen overdose** (30 tablets, 4 hours ago) in a suicide attempt. History: **bipolar I disorder** (3 prior hospitalizations) on lithium until 2 weeks ago when he stopped; **alcohol use disorder** drinking 12 beers/day x 5 years.

**Why this case?** Real psych patients are **medically complex**. David needs simultaneous management of:
• **Medical**: acetaminophen toxicity, impending alcohol withdrawal
• **Psychiatric**: bipolar decompensation, active suicidal ideation
• **Social**: family conflict, job loss, no insurance
• **Legal**: involuntary status pending evaluation

**Your job as the nurse**: integrate **everything** from this NCLEX track — pharmacology, prioritization, therapeutic communication, legal-ethical framework, and the **nursing process** — into one coherent plan that keeps him alive and starts recovery.`,
